146
00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:08.940
And now, fast fact number three.

147
00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:15.900
This episode was Coreza from a production standpoint for several reasons.

148
00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:19.700
First of all, we were starting to cross-board.

149
00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:23.560
That is when you shoot two episodes at once.

150
00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:27.000
And I am very sorry, but I was the reason for the cross-boarding.

151
00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.260
I was getting really close to my due date.

152
00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:36.400
And so, we were shooting both this episode and parts of Pam's replacement all in this

153
00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:36.920
same week.

154
00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:42.400
And they were doing that so that they would shoot me on Mondays and Tuesdays, and then

155
00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:44.720
they would shoot everybody else the rest of the week.

156
00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:49.340
They were always trying to get my work done in the first two days of the week in case I

157
00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:49.960
went into labor.

158
00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:53.980
We didn't know if we were going or coming whenever we did this cross-board stuff.

159
00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.920
And we had done it before, you know?

160
00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:56.460
Oh, yeah.

161
00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.520
But I was like, wait, wait, what am I putting on?

162
00:06:58.660 --> 00:06:59.000
Where am I?

163
00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:00.220
What's the scene?

164
00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:09.640
We also reserved one entire day to shoot the opening skit for the Emmys, the 2011 Emmys.

165
00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.420
I found it on YouTube.

166
00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:12.660
It's really fun.

167
00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:18.400
This is the one where all these different actors from different TV shows came on to the

168
00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:21.260
set of The Office as their characters.

169
00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:21.980
Yeah.

170
00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:22.380
Yeah.

171
00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:27.940
And they were all just like talking about their workplaces as if they were doing a talking

172
00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:28.580
head on The Office.

173
00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:30.200
But there were also little scenes.

174
00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:33.380
So like, for example, at one point, Aaron Paul comes in.

175
00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:38.900
He's being Jesse Pinkman, which it's ironic that later Ryan is Jesse Pinkman for Halloween,

176
00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.280
that this was all happening at the same week.

177
00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:46.360
But Aaron Paul comes on and he's looking for Creed and he's weirded out that there's all

178
00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:48.620
these cameras and Creed's like, don't worry about it.

179
00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:49.420
It's not a big deal.

180
00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:52.020
And then he hands Creed like a little paper bag.

181
00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:54.560
And then Creed yells, I got my crystal meth.

182
00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:59.920
And then as Jesse Pinkman, he's all weirded out and he like runs away.

183
00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:01.920
Aaron Paul is so nice.

184
00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:03.100
So nice.

185
00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:04.300
So nice.

186
00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:06.680
Just a really great guy.

187
00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:07.280
Yeah.

188
00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:12.440
And then there were all kinds of stars, like from 30 Rock and Parks and Recreation and

189
00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:17.100
Mad Men, Law and Order SVU, even Kim Kardashian.

190
00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:22.040
I was talking with Steve Burgess about this and he said that he produced this whole thing

191
00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:26.800
and that most of the actors really did come in and sit in our conference room to do these

192
00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:27.480
talking heads.

193
00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:32.820
And you can see Leslie David Baker sitting in the background of all of these talking heads.

194
00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:38.240
Leslie David Baker, talk about someone who showed up every day and was just such a trooper

195
00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:40.920
because those talking heads sometimes took a really long time.

196
00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:41.400
I know.

197
00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:42.000
He was there.

198
00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:42.860
He was.

199
00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:47.620
There was also a talking head that we did with CeeLo Green, who happened to be a judge

200
00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:48.740
on The Voice that season.

201
00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:52.620
And we brought in one of those giant chairs.

202
00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:57.780
So he's sitting in one of those giant chairs instead of our regular chair.

203
00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:02.540
Steve Burgess said in order to get the chair into the conference room, we had to take down

204
00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:07.380
the entire wall of the conference room, move the chair in and then rebuild it.

205
00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:08.660
Isn't that insane?

206
00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:09.860
That's crazy.

207
00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:14.440
And then I guess there were a few people who were based in New York, like Tracy Morgan

208
00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:16.720
and Mariska Hargitay and Kim Kardashian.

209
00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:21.220
And in that instance, there was a crew in New York who shot them on a green screen.

210
00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:23.620
And then we sort of like inserted our background.

211
00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.900
And then I guess Matt Soane also took a camera around.

212
00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:29.760
He went to the Mad Men set and same thing.

213
00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:33.280
He like set up a green screen because that was the only way to grab, you know, those other

214
00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:34.000
talking heads.

215
00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:36.540
But yeah, this was a big deal.

216
00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:38.480
It took 12 hours, a whole day.

217
00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:39.240
It was our Wednesday.

218
00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:42.340
So we cross-boarded on Monday, Tuesday.

219
00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:46.380
And then we did this crazy Emmy extravaganza on Wednesday.

220
00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:49.960
And then Thursday, Friday was like more of spooked.

221
00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:50.720
It was bonkers.

222
00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:55.040
I was curious to see what was happening during the week that we filmed this.

223
00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:58.260
I always go and check my email, my digital clutter just to see.

224
00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:00.940
And I actually found this in my digital clutter.

225
00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:04.500
Kim Jong emailed me like at 9.52 p.m.

226
00:10:04.780 --> 00:10:06.240
the day before and said,

227
00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:08.660
Hey, Angela, are you going to be on set tomorrow?

228
00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:10.960
I'm going to shoot something on your set for the Emmys.

229
00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:11.920
And I miss you.

230
00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:12.960
I hope all's well.

231
00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:13.820
Will I see you?

232
00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:14.900
XOXO Ken.

233
00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:15.680
No.

234
00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:17.560
Because we have been friends a long time.

235
00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:21.900
We did a movie together years ago called Furry Vengeance, where we played the bad guys.

236
00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:25.340
And I wrote back and I said, Ken, I'm so sorry.

237
00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:26.320
I'm not in today.

238
00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:27.940
I'm bummed that I will miss you.

239
00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:28.660
Have fun.

240
00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:29.280
Aw.

241
00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:32.580
So it was my day off and I did not come in.

242
00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:35.960
Well, Angela, you and I are not in the Emmy extravaganza thing.

243
00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:37.360
I think we had the day off.

244
00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:39.980
And yeah, I don't know why I'm not in it.

245
00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:41.620
I don't know why you're not in it.

246
00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:42.860
Phyllis is also not in it.

247
00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:44.020
And Kate is not in it.

248
00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:47.220
But and Ken Jeong did not make it in either.

249
00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:51.600
So I don't know what he filmed, but I guess it got edited out.

250
00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:52.320
Exactly.

251
00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:54.580
Well, that's all I got for Fast Facts.

252
00:10:54.720 --> 00:11:00.520
Should we take a break and then come back and see Andy is reviewing everyone's costumes

253
00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:02.000
before they can wear them?

254
00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:03.040
Very controlling.

255
00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:04.320
Yeah, he's got rules.

256
